From: Amazing A32 kernel bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] sound: keep GCC maybe-uninitialized diagnostics non-fatal

The vendor sound tree is built with subdir -Werror. GCC 11 emits the same
hardened-usercopy maybe-uninitialized diagnostic already seen in kernel/ when
copy_from_user writes into stack buffers.

Keep the warning visible while preventing this newer compiler diagnostic from
stopping the legacy sound tree build. Other warnings remain fatal.

--- a/sound/Makefile
+++ b/sound/Makefile
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # Makefile for the Linux sound card driver
 #
 
 subdir-ccflags-y += -Werror
+subdir-ccflags-y += $(call cc-option,-Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized)
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_SOUND) += soundcore.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SOUND_PRIME) += oss/
